ion → click e-mail → read/send (check with the listening)"], "X": "لوصف خطوات: first ثم then ثم next ثم after that وأخيرا finally، واستعمل الأمر (imperative).", "EX": [["Rewrite with sequencers: switch on the computer / click on e-mail / sign in.", "First, switch on the computer. Then, sign in. Finally, click on e-mail."], ["What is the imperative form?", "The base form of the verb without a subject: «Click on the icon», «Don't forget»."]], "n": 2, "s": "e", "k": "e1"}, {"m": 1, "i": "⚖️", "t": "Comparing and expressing preferences (e-mail vs snail mail)", "B": [["Comparatives", ["short adj + -er than: fast → faster, cheap → cheaper", "long adj: more interesting than, less personal than, less convenient than", "adverbs: more quickly, more slowly, more clearly"]], ["Preference patterns", ["I prefer e-mailing messages to sending them by ordinary mail.", "I prefer to send messages by snail-mail rather than (send) them by e-mail.", "I prefer e-mail (to snail-mail). This is because…"]], ["Features compared", ["faster / cheaper / more interesting / less personal / less convenient"]]], "K": "prefer + V-ing + to + V-ing ; prefer to + V + rather than + V.", "M": ["Snail-mail = ordinary letters (slow like a snail)", "Irregular: good → better, bad → worse"], "X": "المقارنة: -er than للقصير، more/less ... than للطويل. والتفضيل: prefer X to Y.", "EX": [["Compare: e-mail (fast) / ordinary mail (slow).", "E-mail is faster than ordinary mail."], ["Complete: I prefer reading books ... watching TV.", "to (I prefer reading books to watching TV)."]], "n": 3, "s": "e", "k": "e1"}, {"m": 1, "i": "🎙️", "t": "Requests and intonation; stress in two-syllable words", "B": [["Informal requests", ["Can you speak louder, please? · Can you say that more clearly, please?"]], ["Formal requests", ["Could you go less quickly, please? · Could you speak more slowly, please?", "Formal = Could / Would / Would you mind…"]], ["Stress in 2-syllable words", ["Column A (stress on 1st syllable): browser, modem, cursor, pointer, windows, floppy, icon, keyboard", "Column B (stress on 2nd): erase, escape, protect, display, remove, connect", "Nouns usually stressed on the first syllable; many verbs on the second"]]], "K": "Requests: Can (informal) / Could (formal) + please; stress the right syllable.", "M": ["Hidden message 1: «Your floppy disk contains a virus. Remove it from my computer.»", "Intonation at the end of requests is usually rising (↗) when polite — check with the recording"], "X": "Can للطلب غير الرسمي وCould للرسمي. وفي الكلمات ذات المقطعين: الأسماء غالبا تُنبَر على الأول والأفعال على الثاني.", "EX": [["Make formal: «Can you type more quickly?»", "Could you type more quickly, please?"], ["Where is the stress in «browser» and «erase»?", "browser: first syllable (BROW-ser); erase: second (e-RASE)."]], "n": 4, "s": "e", "k": "e1"}, {"m": 2, "i": "✉️", "t": "Reading an e-mail: Kirsi's letter to Amel", "B": [["Structure of an e-mail", ["To / From / Subject / Cc / Bcc / Attached", "Salutation (Dear Amel) → body → closing (Keep in touch) → name → P.S."]], ["Content", ["Kirsi is Finnish, 16, wants to be a journalist; she must study six more years", "Weekdays: gets up early, classes 8:30–12 and 2–4, lunch at canteen or fast food, revises until ~10 p.m.; rarely goes out at the weekend", "Family: Mum (housewife), Dad (electrician), brother Jari (14); a dog and a parrot", "Lives in Tikkakoski (4,000 inhabitants), near Jyväskylä (63,000); Finland: 7 million people"]], ["Finland", ["In the north of Europe, near the Arctic Circle", "Famous for saunas and lakes; winter terrible, summer fairly cool"]]], "K": "In an e-mail she introduces herself, her routine, family and country.", "M": ["Pronoun reference: «your» = Amel's; «myself» = Kirsi; «them» = the parrot and the dog; «It» = Jyväskylä / Finland", "Sauna = hot steam bath"], "X": "رسالة بريد إلكتروني: تعرّف الكاتبة بنفسها وروتينها وعائلتها وبلدها (فنلندا).", "EX": [["How often does Kirsi go out at the weekend?", "Rarely: she