emperatures»"], "X": "الصفات العادية تأخذ very/quite، أما الصفات القصوى (huge, freezing, terrible) فلا نقول معها very.", "EX": [["Replace with an extreme adjective: «very bad».", "terrible / appalling."], ["Is «very boiling» correct?", "No: «boiling» is extreme; say «absolutely boiling» or «very hot»."]], "n": 7, "s": "e", "k": "e2"}, {"m": 2, "i": "📝", "t": "Writing a reply and introducing your country", "B": [["Plan of a reply", ["A. Say thank you; introduce yourself briefly", "B. Describe your regular activities (frequency adverbs)", "C. Introduce your family", "D. Introduce your country (degree adverbs + adjectives)"]], ["Useful structures", ["It's situated in / located in North Africa.", "To the east, it's bordered by…", "It has a population of… / an area of…", "It's 2,000 km long from north to south.", "The average temperature in summer is more/less than…", "It's famous / well-known for…"]], ["Prepositions of place", ["in the north, to the east of, at, on the coast, in the mountains"]]], "K": "Reply: thank → yourself → routine → family → country.", "M": ["Correct your mistakes, exchange drafts with a partner, then write the final version", "Start: Thank you for your e-mail. My name is…"], "X": "خطة الرد: شكر، تعريف، أنشطة يومية، العائلة، ثم وصف بلدك بصيغ مثل situated in وbordered by وfamous for.", "EX": [["Write one sentence about Algeria with «situated».", "Algeria is situated in North Africa."], ["How do you say the east border?", "To the east, it is bordered by Tunisia and Libya."]], "n": 8, "s": "e", "k": "e2"}, {"m": 3, "i": "📞", "t": "Telephone tactics", "B": [["Answering", ["At home: Hello. · In business: Good morning, SEK Company, can I help you? / Bob Karl speaking.", "Numbers: 7214422 = seven two one double four double two"]], ["Asking for someone", ["Hello, is Karima there? It's her brother. / I'm… / My name's…", "Can/May/Could I speak to…, please? · I would like to speak to…", "B: Who's calling / speaking, please?"]], ["Waiting / absent", ["A moment, please. · Hold on / hang on. · Could you hold on, please? · I'll see if he's in.", "I'm sorry / I'm afraid he's on holiday / out at the moment / away for the weekend."]], ["Messages and goodbye", ["Would you like to leave a message? Can I take a message?", "Please ask her to call me. My number's… · I'll call her later.", "Wrong number: No, it isn't. You've got the wrong number.", "Goodbye (business); See you on Monday, bye (home)."]]], "K": "Polite phone English: Could you hold on? / I'm afraid he isn't here at the moment.", "M": ["Exercise answers: A (027322) = zero-two-seven-three-double two · B = Who's calling, please? · C = Could you hold on, please? · D = I'm afraid, he isn't here at the moment", "«Speaking» = this is the person you want"], "X": "عبارات المكالمات: Who's calling? Could you hold on? I'm afraid he's out. Can I take a message?", "EX": [["What do you say when the caller forgets to give his name?", "Who's calling, please?"], ["The person is out. What does the receptionist say?", "I'm afraid he's out at the moment. Would you like to leave a message?"]], "n": 9, "s": "e", "k": "e3"}, {"m": 3, "i": "🎉", "t": "Invitations: accepting and refusing", "B": [["Formal invitation (text 1)", ["Tom and Edora Smith would like to invite you to their HOUSE WARMING on Saturday 12th November, from 7.00 p.m. to 9.00 p.m. We look forward to showing you our new house. R.S.V.P.", "House warming = party to celebrate moving into a new house", "R.S.V.P. = Répondez s'il vous plaît (reply please); used in English because it is the formal convention"]], ["Informal invitation (text 2)", ["Dear Peter, We'll celebrate Anne's success at her exams on Thursday 21st, from 6 to 9 p.m. Come and share with us the celebration if you're free. Regards, Sam"]], ["Acceptance (text 3)", ["Thank you very much for your invitation. It will be a real pleasure for me to meet you again. I am looking forward to seeing you on Friday at 8 p.m."]], ["Refusal (text 4)", ["Thank you very much for your 