 "e3"}, {"m": 4, "i": "🎯", "t": "Expressing purpose: to / in order to / so as to", "B": [["Affirmative", ["We use to, in order to, so as to to express purpose.", "I sent her a message to / in order to / so as to congratulate her."]], ["Negative", ["not to · in order not to · so as not to", "I sent her a message not to invite her, but to congratulate her.", "So as not to be late, you have to start now. / You have to start now in order not to be late."]], ["Position", ["At the beginning or in the middle of the sentence", "«To» alone cannot start a sentence in the formal way with «not»: use in order not to / so as not to"]]], "K": "purpose = to / in order to / so as to (+ verb); negative = in order not to / so as not to.", "M": ["Exercise: (1) to (2) In order to / So as to (3) to (4) not to (5) so as not to / in order not to", "Link words answer the question «why?»"], "X": "للتعبير عن الغرض: to / in order to / so as to. والنفي: in order not to / so as not to.", "EX": [["Combine: She took the bus. She wanted to arrive earlier.", "She took the bus so as to arrive earlier."], ["Complete: Read silently ... disturb the others.", "so as not to / in order not to."]], "n": 13, "s": "e", "k": "e4"}, {"m": 4, "i": "🪞", "t": "Reflexive pronouns", "B": [["Table", ["I → me → my → myself · you → you → your → yourself · he → him → his → himself", "she → her → her → herself · it → it → its → itself", "we → us → our → ourselves · you → you → your → yourselves · they → them → their → themselves"]], ["Use", ["When the object of the verb is the same as the subject", "I have to introduce myself."]], ["Exercise answers", ["You have to introduce yourself · Farid admires himself · Amel describes herself", "Karim and Rachid have to clean themselves · My friend and I enjoyed ourselves · The parrot is looking at itself"]]], "K": "Subject = object → reflexive pronoun (myself, himself, themselves…).", "M": ["Singular: -self · plural: -selves", "enjoy yourself = have a good time"], "X": "الضمير الانعكاسي عندما يكون الفاعل والمفعول نفس الشخص: myself, yourself, himself...", "EX": [["Fill: The parrot is talking to ... .", "itself."], ["Fill: We enjoyed ... at the party.", "ourselves."]], "n": 14, "s": "e", "k": "e4"}, {"m": 4, "i": "📏", "t": "Obligation: must / have to / mustn't / needn't / had to", "B": [["Obligation", ["must and have to (affirmative and question): You must start from here. Do I have to start from here?"]], ["Prohibition", ["mustn't: You mustn't switch on the computer before quitting the program."]], ["No obligation", ["needn't / don't have to / doesn't have to: You needn't send a message. Just phone them."]], ["Past", ["No past form of must: use had to (obligation) and didn't have to (no obligation)", "I missed the bus yesterday. So I had to walk to school.", "Future: will have to"]]], "K": "must/have to = necessary; mustn't = forbidden; needn't/don't have to = not necessary.", "M": ["School rules: We must wear a uniform. We mustn't use phones in class. We needn't come on Friday.", "mustn't ≠ don't have to !"], "X": "must وhave to للإلزام، mustn't للمنع، needn't وdon't have to لعدم اللزوم، وhad to للماضي.", "EX": [["Difference: «You mustn't go» / «You don't have to go».", "mustn't = it is forbidden; don't have to = it is not necessary (you can go if you want)."], ["Put in the past: «I must walk to school.»", "I had to walk to school."]], "n": 15, "s": "e", "k": "e4"}, {"m": 4, "i": "🔤", "t": "Articles: a / an / the / zero article", "B": [["Indefinite (a, an)", ["Only before singular countable nouns: a photo, an e-mail", "First reference"]], ["Definite (the)", ["Before common nouns (singular/plural, countable/uncountable)", "Second reference: I received a photo. The photo is beautiful."]], ["Zero article (Φ)", ["No article: plural or uncountable (photos, paper), languages, subjects, names (In Arabic, Physics and English)", "Some/any = plural of a/an: I have sent some e-mails. Have you received any?"]]], "K": "a/an = first mention; the = known/second mention; Φ = general plural/uncountable.", "M": ["Dialogue sample: My father is an engineer and my mother is a housewife.", "North Africa, Algeria → Φ (names of places); the Arctic Circle → the"], "X": "a/an للمفرد المعدود أول مرة، the للمعروف، وبدون أداة مع الجمع والمواد العامة وأسماء اللغات والمواد.", "EX": [["Fill: I have received ... e-mail. ... e-mail is from Kirsi.", "an / The."], ["a or an: ... engineer, ... photo, ... hour.", "an engineer, a photo, an hour."]], "n": 16, "s": "e", "k": "e4"}, {"m": 4, "i": "📅", "t": "Prepositions and time: in / on / at / up / down / from…to / until", "B": [["Phrasal prepositions (computers)", ["switch on · click on · sign in/up · move down the page · log off"]], ["from … to", ["Gives periods of time (past → future): from 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. · from Saturday to Thursday · from 1954 to 1962"]], ["until", ["Gives end points: until 2015 · until December · until Monday · until 5 o'clock", "I waited for the message until 9 o'clock and I left."]], ["Example (Tower of London ad)", ["Open until 31 Oct: Tues–Sat 09.00–18.00; from 1 Nov: closes at 17.00; last admission 1 hour before closing"]]], "K": "from…to = period; until = end point.", "M": ["Exercise 4: switch on · click on · sign in · sign up · move down", "Note: The Tower of London will be open for visitors from Tuesday to Saturday until 6 p.m."], "X": "from ... to لفترة زمنية، وuntil لنقطة النهاية.", "EX": [["Complete: The shop is open ... 9 a.m. ... 5 p.m.", "from … to."], ["Complete: I'll wait ... six o'clock.", "until."]], "n": 17, "s": "e", "k": "e4"}, {"m": 4, "i": "👫", "t": "both…and / either…or / neither…nor", "B": [["Patterns", ["both … and … : both clean and beautiful", "either … or … : either today or tomorrow", "neither … nor … : neither smokes nor gambles (negative meaning, positive verb)"]], ["With of", ["both of / either of / neither of + the, these, those, my, your, them, us…", "Both of them are Jari's pets. Neither of them really belongs to me."]], ["Exercise 2 answers", ["Neither Hichem nor Fatima is late for class.", "Both Farid and Foued like learning languages.", "We can leave either today or tomorrow.", "Our classroom is both clean and beautiful.", "I neither smoke nor play cards."]]], "K": "Both + and = the two; either + or = one of two; neither + nor = none of the two.", "M": ["Never use «not» with neither…nor", "Kirsi's e-mail: «neither of them really belongs to me» / «Both of them are Jari's pets»"], "X": "both…and للاثنين معا، either…or لأحدهما، neither…nor لا هذا ولا ذاك.", "EX": [["Join: «I don't smoke. I don't play cards.»", "I neither smoke nor play cards."], ["Join: «Farid likes languages. Foued likes languages.»", "Both Farid and Foued like languages."]], "n": 18, "s": "e", "k": "e4"}, {"m": 5, "i": "📄", "t": "Letter of application and résumé (CV)", "B": [["Help wanted ad (camp leaders)", ["Job requires tolerance, patience, open-mindedness, cheerfulness and understanding", "Duties: dealing with children, organising and participating in daily activities", "Write with must / have to: Candidates must be patient. They have to deal with children."]], ["Letter of application (Joy Parfit)", ["Re: Camp leader; Dear Mr Armstrong", "§1 where you saw the ad · §2 your qualifications and activities (junior at Thomas Jefferson High School, photography and music clubs)", "§3 your age and experience (looks after her brothers and sisters) · §4 availability and references (two teachers)", "Yours sincerely"]], ["Résumé headings", ["Name (first, middle, last) · Address · Place of birth · Age · Education · Languages", "Previous work experience · Interests · References"]], ["Replies", ["Offer: I am writing to inform you that I am able to offer you the position as camp leader.", "Thanks: Thank you for offering me the post of camp leader. · Thank you for your letter of June 6.", "Interview: I should like you to come for an interview on Friday June 12."]]], "K": "Application letter: where you saw the ad, who you are, your experience, availability, references.", "M": ["Joy has a good chance: she is tolerant, likes meeting people, looks after children", "Résumé = curriculum vitae (CV)"], "X": "رسالة الترشح: مصدر الإعلان، تعريف بالنفس، الخبرات، الجاهزية، المراجع. وللسيرة الذاتية عناوين ثابتة.", "EX": [["Write the opening of a letter of application.", "I have seen your advertisement for camp leaders in the newspaper and would like to apply for the job."], ["List four headings of a résumé.", "Name, address, education, languages (also place of birth, age, experience, interests, references)."]], "n": 19, "s": "e", "k": "e5"}, {"m": 5, "i": "☎️", "t": "Telephone problems: work it out", "B": [["Common problems", ["Wrong number · bad line · line engaged · can't hear / understand · phones out of order"]], ["Useful replies", ["Sorry, you've got the wrong number.", "No, I can't. It's a bad line.", "My line was engaged.", "Our phones were out of order all morning.", "My English is not very good."]], ["Solutions in the book (dialogues 1–5)", ["1 → c (wrong number) · 2 → a (bad line) · 3 → b (line engaged)", "4 → e (My English is not very good) · 5 → d (phones out of order)"]]], "K": "Solve phone problems politely: apologise, explain, offer a solution.", "M": ["Could you speak up, please? · Sorry, what did you say? I didn't catch that…", "Try his mobile phone."], "X": "مشاكل الهاتف: رقم خاطئ، خط سيئ، الخط مشغول. واعتذر ثم اشرح السبب.", "EX": [["What do you say if you can't hear?", "Could you speak up, please? I can't hear you very well."], ["A: I couldn't get through. B: What was the problem? A: ...", "My line was engaged. (or: The phones were out of order.)"]], "n": 20, "s": "e", "k": "e5"}, {"m": 5, "i": "🛠️", "t": "Project workshop: job application booklet / Internet user's guide", "B": [["Project 1: Job application booklet", ["Purpose: a booklet for teenage job seekers", "Include: adverts with job descriptions, phone enquiries, résumés/CVs, letters of reference, letters of application, replies (positive, negative), letters of acceptance"]], ["Project 2: Internet user's guide for beginners", ["Description of a workstation / PC (Personal Computer)", "Instructions (opening an e-mail account, homepage…)", "Maintenance tips (no smoking, protection from dust)", "Tips for solving problems when the PC goes wrong · manners when using the Internet"]], ["Round-up", ["Correct your mistakes · exchange booklets with other groups · display your booklets"]]], "K": "Project = a job application booklet OR an Internet user's guide.", "M": ["Unit 1 project: working in groups", "Netiquette = manners on the Internet"], "X": "مشروع الوحدة: كتيّب للتوظيف أو دليل استعمال الإنترنت للمبتدئين، ثم تصحيح وتبادل وعرض.", "EX": [["Name three items of the job application booklet.", "Adverts, résumés/CVs, letters of application (also reference letters, replies, acceptance letters)."], ["What should an Internet user's guide include?", "Description of a PC, instructions, maintenance tips, problem-solving tips, and Internet manners."]], "n": 21, "s": "e", "k": "e5"}, {"m": 5, "i": "✅", "t": "Check your progress: recipe e-mail, grammar review and glossary", "B": [["Indian Pudding e-mail", ["Cheyenne → Sihem: she sends the recipe she talked about; ingredients: corn meal, hot milk, sugar, baking soda, salt, ginger, cinnamon, molasses, cold milk, whipped cream, nutmeg", "Rewrite the recipe with first, then, next, after that, finally"]], ["Key answers", ["Questions: How often does she go to school by bus? · What time does she go to bed? · What do they like playing? · Where is Algeria situated? · How often does he have dinner at home?", "Complaint letter: I am writing (1) to complain… (2) So as not to / In order not to let the situation worsen… (3) so as to / in order to discuss…"]], ["Skills to self-assess", ["Describe regular activities · describe a process · express obligation · invitations/apologies · enquiry · résumé · application · phone conversation · purpose · stress · degree adverbs/extreme adjectives"]], ["Glossary (selection)", ["abbreviation = اختصار · apology = اعتذار · enclose = يرفق · enquiry = استفسار", "fee = رسوم · prospectus = دليل · keypal = صديق مراسلة · open-minded = متفتح العقل · tolerant = متسامح"]]], "K": "Review: sequencers, frequency adverbs, modals, purpose, both/either/neither, formal requests.", "M": ["Formal requests: Could you dictate the message to me, please? · Could you pass me that book, please?", "Headlines: Brilliant result · Freezing temperatures · Stunning places · Appalling standards"], "X": "مراجعة نهاية الوحدة: كل القواعد في الوحدة 1 مع قاموس مصغر (English/Arabic).", "EX": [["Write questions: «She rarely goes to school by bus.»", "How often does she go to school by bus?"], ["Use must and have to for the ad (Camp leaders).", "Candidates must be well-organised. They have to speak good English."]], "n": 22, "s": "e", "k": "e5"}, {"m": 6, "i": "🧞", "t": "Unit 2 preview and Sindbad the Sailor (Arabian Nights)", "B": [["Unit 2 aims", ["Listen and respond to a tale; express likes and dislikes about literary works", "Read a blurb and a literary portrait; describe people's physical appearance and personality", "Read a street map; ask for and give directions; past continuous and past simple with when / while; besides / beside; who / whom / which", "Project: a book review, a writers' sketch book, a family history project or a story book"]], ["Arabian Nights tales", ["Aladdin and the Magic Lamp · Ali Baba and the Forty Thieves · The Voyages of Sindbad the Sailor · The Fisherman and the Jinnee · King Shahryar and his Brother"]], ["Sindbad's first voyage", ["B) He inherited money, spent it quickly, became poor → decided to be a merchant sailor", "D) Travelled from Baghdad to Basra, sailed down the Shatt Al-Arab and through the Gulf to the Far East", "E) Stopped on an «island» for fresh water: it was a whale", "F) Reached a real island; the king's horseman helped him · A) took him to a cave, gave food and water · C) one day at the harbour he saw boxes with his name on them"]]], "K": "Narrate a tale in the past simple with time markers.", "M": ["Story picture order (probable): B → D → E → F → A → C — check with the listening", "Start: I'm Sindbad the sailor. I've made seven voyages…"], "X": "حكاية السندباد: تُروى بالماضي البسيط مع روابط زمنية (one day, so, actually).", "EX": [["Put in the past: «I inherit money and spend it.»", "I inherited money and spent it."], ["Why did Sindbad become a merchant sailor?", "He had become poor after spending his inheritance, so he wanted to make money."]], "n": 23, "s": "e", "k": "e6"}, {"m": 6, "i": "🔊", "t": "Pronunciation: final -ed and stress in three-syllable words", "B": [["-ed endings", ["/t/ after voiceless sounds: stopped", "/d/ after voiced sounds: travelled, sailed, climbed", "/ɪd/ after t or d: started, landed"]], ["3-syllable adjectives", ["Stress on the 2nd syllable (o 0 o): dramatic, fantastic, relaxing, exciting, depressing", "Stress on the 1st syllable (0 o o): saddening, magical, wonderful"]], ["Hidden message", ["/aɪ laɪk ðə bʊk bɪˈkɒz ɪt hæs gʊd ˈkærəktəz/ = I like the book because it has good characters."]]], "K": "-ed = /t/, /d/ or /ɪd/ depending on the last sound; learn the stress of adjectives.", "M": ["Voiceless sounds: p, k, f, s, ʃ, tʃ → /t/", "Verbs ending in t or d add a syllable: /ɪd/"], "X": "نطق -ed: /t/ بعد الأصوات المهموسة، /d/ بعد المجهورة، /ɪd/ بعد t وd.", "EX": [["How is «stopped» pronounced at the end?", "/t/ (stopped = /stɒpt/)."], ["How is «landed» pronounced at the end?", "/ɪd/ (two syllables: /ˈlændɪd/)."]], "n": 24, "s": "e", "k": "e6"}, {"m": 6, "i": "📚", "t": "Likes and dislikes about books; writing a book review", "B": [["Favourable", ["an absorbing / powerful / exciting / delightful / enjoyable / charming / striking / superb / fascinating / lively / gripping + story/characters/setting"]], ["Unfavourable", ["aggressive · inconsistent/flat · confusing · lazy · careless · boring · conventional · sentimental · depressing · appalling · saddening · difficult"]], ["Dialogue", ["What's your favourite book? → Dracula (Bram Stoker)", "Why are you fond of it / keen on it? → I like it because it tells an absorbing story / it has powerful characters"]], ["Review model (Ms Wiz Loves Dracula)", ["Title, authors, publisher, price, ISBN, reviewer", "I like the story very much because it is full of suspense. Besides, its characters are very funny. I recommend the story to every reader who is fond of magic."]]], "K": "Say what you like using aspects: characters, narrative, setting.", "M": ["Books shown: Peter Pan, Treasure Island, Tom Sawyer, Dracula", "I recommend… to every reader who is fond of…"], "X": "للتعبير عن إعجابك: absorbing, powerful, gripping. وعن عدمه: boring, depressing. واختم بـ I recommend.", "EX": [["Give two reasons to like a book.", "It tells an absorbing story and it has powerful characters."], ["What is a book review?", "A short text giving details of a book and the reviewer's opinion, ending with a recommendation."]], "n": 25, "s": "e", "k": "e6"}, {"m": 6, "i": "📖", "t": "Reading a blurb and a literary portrait (Things Fall Apart)", "B": [["Blurb", ["The text on the back cover of a book: author information, short comment, ISBN, publisher; it is included to attract readers", "Chinua Achebe is a Nigerian author; Things Fall Apart tells of the tragedy of Okonkwo, an important man of the Igbo tribe, before and with the arrival of the white coloniser"]], ["Okonkwo", ["Appearance: tall and huge, very dark complexion, wide nose, bushy eyebrows, fierce look", "Personality: hard worker, brave, liked action, took up arms against the British invaders", "Famous after beating Amalinze the Cat at 18"]], ["Unoka (his father)", ["Appearance: thin, handsome man with a gentle look, always in his agbada (Nigerian dress)", "Personality: lazy, improvident, a coward; liked playing the flute, preferred music to war"]], ["Language", ["Past simple for a past story/portrait", "have + features: He had bushy eyebrows. · wear: He was always in/wearing his agbada.", "with / in: a girl with a round face; a lady in a pink dress"]]], "K": "Okonkwo is the strong hard-working hero; his father Unoka is lazy and gentle.", "M": ["Synonym: well-known = famous · gentle ≠ fierce · coward ≠ brave", "Setting = place and time of the story"], "X": "البلورب هو نص الغلاف الخلفي للتشويق. وصف أوكونكو (قوي شجاع) مقابل أبيه أونوكا (كسول جبان).", "EX": [["Join with «with»: «She was a pretty girl. She had a round face.»", "She was a pretty girl with a round face."], ["Join with «in»: «She was an elderly lady. She was wearing a pink dress.»", "She was an elderly lady in a pink dress."]], "n": 26, "s": "e", "k": "e6"}, {"m": 6, "i": "🧑", "t": "Describing people (tactics summary)", "B": [["Order of description", ["Age: in her early twenties, about thirty, middle-aged", "Height: tall / small / of average height", "Build: plump, overweight, athletic, stocky, skinny, slim, broad-shouldered, well-built"]], ["Features", ["Hair: length, style, colour — long curly black hair", "Eyes: size, shape, colour — small round grey eyes; sparkling, twinkling, dreamy, worried", "Face: round / square / oval; thick lips; high cheekbones; bald; pointed chin", "Skin: pale, tanned, olive, dark; fair complexion"]], ["Extras", ["Clothes order: age, shape, colour, origin, material — old tight blue Italian nylon trousers", "Distinguishing features: scar, birthmark, mole, beard, tattoo, glasses; voice: stutter, lisp, deep, soft", "Character: anxious, cheerful, arrogant, relaxed, aggressive"]]], "K": "Describe in order: age, height, build, hair, eyes, face, skin, clothes, features, character.", "M": ["Hair order: length, style, colour", "Opinion before size before age before shape before colour… (adjective order)"], "X": "وصف الأشخاص بترتيب: العمر، الطول، البنية، الشعر، العيون، الوجه، البشرة، الملابس، العلامات المميزة، الطبع.", "EX": [["Describe a man: tall / bald / beard / glasses.", "He was a tall bald man with a beard and glasses."], ["Give the right order: «hair: black, long, curly».", "long curly black hair (length, style, colour)."]], "n": 27, "s": "e", "k": "e6"}, {"m": 6, "i": "⏳", "t": "Time expressions and narrating in the past", "B": [["Time expressions", ["yesterday · two days / months / years / centuries ago · last week / weekend / month / year", "in November, in 1954, in the nineteenth century · on July 5th, on Monday · at the age of eighteen", "three days / years later · when"]], ["Past simple", ["Regular: -ed (travelled, started); irregular: won, became, spent, went", "Example: At the age of eighteen, he won a wrestling match against Amalinze."]], ["Past tense in the text", ["The text uses the past simple because it describes events and people of the past"]]], "K": "Use the past simple with past time expressions (ago, last, yesterday, in 1954).", "M": ["ago comes after the time: two years ago", "when + past simple = at the time of an action"], "X": "الماضي البسيط مع تعابير الزمن الماضي: yesterday, ago, last, in, on, at the age of.", "EX": [["Write a sentence with «ago».", "He won the match twenty years ago."], ["Which tense is used to describe Okonkwo's life and why?", "The past simple, because the story and the events are finished in the past."]], "n": 28, "s": "e", "k": "e6"}, {"m": 6, "i": "🏭", "t": "Coketown (Hard Times, Dickens) and guided story-telling", "B": [["Coketown", ["A town of red brick, machinery and tall chimneys; smoke like interminable serpents; a black canal and a river running purple with ill-smelling dye", "The machines worked up and down monotonously like a melancholy elephant", "Streets and people all very like one another; they worked in the textile factories", "No leisure centre or public library for children: it was a depressing, noisy, boring town"]], ["Literary devices", ["Comparisons (similes): like the painted face of a savage; like a melancholy elephant", "Dirtiness (§1), monotony (§2) and boredom (§3) are conveyed by description and repetition"]], ["Write a scene (model)", ["Name and what it was like (analogies)", "Where it was situated: in the east/centre of the country, on the Mediterranean coast, in the mountains, in the Sahara…", "Facilities, sights, sounds, smells; number of people and their jobs; what life was like"]], ["Guided story telling", ["Begin: A long time ago, there was an elderly lady living in a cottage in the forest with her granddaughter.", "Middle: One day, a young horseman stopped at the cottage… (what he looked like, who he was, where from, why he stopped, what happened)"]]], "K": "Setting a scene: place, appearance, sensory details, people, atmosphere.", "M": ["Story: The lion asks «Who is the king of the jungle?» — the elephant throws him against a tree", "Moral: don't be rough with those stronger than you"], "X": "وصف المكان في القصة: الموقع والمظهر والحواس والسكان والجو العام، مع تشبيهات.", "EX": [["What is Coketown compared to?", "Its smoke to serpents, its machines to a melancholy elephant, its colour to the painted face of a savage."], ["Was Coketown a good place to live? Why?", "No: it was dirty, noisy, monotonous and had no leisure facilities for children."]], "n": 29, "s": "e", "k": "e6"}];
